{"reference":"Jeremiah 21","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":21,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Jeremiah in Its Larger Book","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Jeremiah 21 belongs to a book that brings together varied kinds of material, including poetry, prose sermons, narratives, letters, headings, repeated accounts, restoration collections, oracles concerning nations, and an appendix. A practical outline places chapters 2–25 together, but that arrangement does not settle questions about how the book took shape. This broader observation is disputed, so it is best treated as a guide to the book’s varied form rather than a firm explanation of this chapter’s composition.","confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed","provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_021_5e27c37ce281c86af8e82848"]}]}],"generated_metadata":null}